Z||000000||Loki||03-22-2001||12:05 AM||||Did the Formula have all the same options as the GT?<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR> <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||03-22-2001||01:04 AM||||Nope.  I'm not 100% sure on this, so don't quote me.. but I don't think you could get performance sound, leather, lumbar, and maybe a few other things.  A wing came standard on the Formula, though.  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||rodmcneill||03-22-2001||01:15 AM||||Electric mirrors were not available as an option.||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||03-22-2001||01:16 AM||||Formulas are coupes with a $2000 option package.  Mechanically they are identical to the GT, but the body and interior are basic coupe fare.  You could not get all of the "premium" goodies. <P>Things like power mirrors, leather seats, leather steering wheel, leather shift knob/handle, lumbar seat, EQ radio, subwoofer, 2-tone dash and power trunk release were not available as options on the Formula.<P>The rear spoiler was standard......it was included in the Formula option package.  The Indy pace car was the only other Fiero to have a spoiler as standard equipment.<P>  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||rodmcneill||03-22-2001||01:19 AM||||I have also heard the seat fabric was different, not as durable as the GT's. My 200th post YEAH!!||||reg||1
Z||000005||mrfiero||03-22-2001||01:49 AM||||The seat material is the same as the base coupe, which is better than previous years but not as durable as the '88 GT material.  I have owned numerous '88 GT's (8 or 9) and have never seen one rip (we're talking cloth here......the leather seats will wear and tear)  ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Songman||03-22-2001||01:56 AM||||I'm learning something here...<P>I thought you could order the goodies on a Formula but it just didn't come standard... hmmmmm.....<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||1
Z||000007||mrfiero||03-22-2001||03:00 AM||||Most Formulas were basically stripped.....no power options at all.  This  was to get someone into a V-6 powered Fiero as cheaply as possible.  The base coupe price in '88 was $8999, the Formula was $10999 (hence a $2000 option) and the GT was $13999.  <P>As more options were ordered on a Formula it became a better deal to buy a GT, which is what GM wanted.  They preferred to sell more GT's, since they had a higher profit margin.  <P>A fully loaded Formula consists of: pw, pdl, rear de-fog., air, cruise, tilt, sunroof or T-Top and of course an auto tranny (although most people would consider a 5-sp., with the other options, as being loaded).<P>There are some people who insist that they have seen a Formula with power mirrors or other premium options.  There is a slim possibility that a few were produced, but I have never seen one.  Generally speaking, a Formula could only come with the above options. ||||reg||1
Z||000008||fiero56||03-22-2001||08:03 AM||||Speaking with Ed parks last month at The Fiero Factory, Ed mentioned there were a few Formulas that left with non-standard factory options. Like PM, trunk release, etc. A quick check of my Spotters guide confirmed this. <P>If anyone remmebers the "new" Orange Formula at the meet last year, Ed says that was oneof the rare "all options from the factory" Formulas.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Loki||03-22-2001||09:59 AM||||Cool, thanx for the info... Im looking to get an 88 due to all the things  being "better" BUt dont like that fastback. So in the future when I get an 88GT ill be finding someon who wants to swap rear ends   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/headshot.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Raydar||03-22-2001||12:12 PM||||According to the Spotters Guide, there were also a handful of Formulas sold with the subwoofer system. <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000011||Fformula88||03-22-2001||07:40 PM||||Here are the options that couldn't be ordered on Formula's (special factory cars aside)<P>From the option groups:  Power Mirrors<BR>Additional Options: Luggage rack (rather have the wing!) <BR>Subwoffer Stereo (all others available, inc. Stereo w/ EQ)<BR>Gold diamond spoke wheels<BR>Leather Seats<P>There isn't a big option difference if you loaded it out.  <BR>My Formula wasn't heavily optioned, but still hit an MSRP of $13,287.00, including opt grp 1sB, auto tranny, mats, ETR stereo, rear defogger.  I am still without power windows/locks, sunroof, and an EQ radio.  Its not badly optioned, although no GT.||||reg||1
